    "introduction": "InterContinental Hotels Group, or IHG, operates a portfolio of hotel brands including Holiday Inn, InterContinental and Crowne Plaza. Much of its business involves franchising brands or managing hotels owned by third parties, rather than owning every hotel building itself. It earns fees linked to hotel activity and management arrangements, supported by reservation systems, loyalty programmes and brand standards. Hotel owners gain distribution and operating support, while guests receive recognisable brands across destinations. Performance depends on travel demand, room rates and the number of hotels using its systems. Maintaining service consistency and attracting owners to develop or convert hotels are important to expansion.",
